# Pure-kernel unit tests: a finished sentence is clean, a byte-budget cut is caught at both carry
# sites and through trailing whitespace, an odd fence run is an unclosed fence, a member named in
# supersedes but never carried is caught, a topic only the members carry is reported ONCE with its
# evidence, and a collapsed walk fails closed instead of reporting a clean corpus. All proven
# WITHOUT a filesystem, on fixtures whose ids carry no governed ADR shape.
rust_test(
    name = "check-apex-gist-integrity-unittest",
    srcs = glob(["src/**/*.rs", "**/*.json"]),
    crate = "check_apex_gist_integrity",
    crate_root = "src/lib.rs",
    visibility = ["PUBLIC"],
    deps = [],
)

